=== 6. V3: the excuse oracle is external now, and I checked it independently

Code read: the integral and identity arms no longer call differentiate,
verify_identity or eval_at to excuse a Verified mutant (grep of
tests/verifier.rs shows no such call in the mutation test); they look the
mutant up in the fixture (tests/verifier.rs:490, 634), and the equation arms
look the mutated root up in equivalent_roots (551).

The fixture is generated by SymPy, but the risk V3 named is the opposite
direction: an over-inclusive list excuses a false Verified silently. I wrote my
own parser and my own equivalence decision (check_fixture.py: parse with SymPy,
then simplify(d/dx mutant - integrand) == 0; or residual at a root), importing
nothing from generate.py and nothing from mathd:

fixture: mathd/fixtures/verifier.json
integral equivalent_mutants checked : 43
equation equivalent_roots checked   : 20
symbolic simplify inconclusive      : 0
NOT GENUINELY EQUIVALENT: 0  (all 63 entries agree with SymPy)
STATUS=0

43 + 20 = 63 = the excused count in the matrix. So every excuse is correct
today, and the list is not padded.

Wiring check (break F8, below): emptying those 63 fixture entries makes the
mutation test fail with 63 false Verified and exit 1. The oracle is load
bearing, not decorative.

